\f1\fs22 \'93\'85 where you expect to be lauded and fed,\'94 Dunhilton rejoined.\
\'93Even so, CEO, Sunday is a day for quiet reflection on charts and numbers, and to give thanks that wealth accrues to those virtuous enough to deserve it,\'94 Moral Observance ventured.\
\'93Well, perhaps church should not be on the morning after Saturday night,\'94 Dunhilton baited. \'93Now, if you could focus your attentions on preventing lewd thoughts of\'97oh I dunno, sedition\'85\'94\
Moral Observance blanched and belched. His morning\'92s breakfast degustation wasn\'92t agreeing with him.\
\'93\'85 attempted murder \'85\'94 Dunhilton went on slowly, extracting the greatest unease from Moral Observance. \'93\'85 gate-crashing a private church service\'97a Holy Joint Venture, no less \'85 crimes against music\'85 If you could have clamped down on just one of these social ills, I might not be calling a cabinet meeting during church hours.\'94\
\'93Yes, your Serene Corporateness.\'94 Moral Observance tried to look abashed, but his eyes intransigently trailed towards the plate of tantalising pastries on the board table. They were just far enough out of his reach; if he wanted one he\'92d need to make an indecorous lunge for the plate.\
Dunhilton took a pastry, and returned the plate just a little more out of Moral Observance\'92s reach. He surveyed the directors present. Behind their grim smiles he could see them rehearsing their craven, self-interested proposals in their heads; he\'92d heard them all before. Corrections wanted fresh criminals for private prisons. Housing salivated over dense Ghetto redevelopment. Tourism wanted his Elvi World theme park. Defence wanted to conscript them for Indonesian palm oil fantasies. These were all excellent ideas, the CEO conceded, which together could in the fullness of time yield a fully integrated master plan of synergistic opportunities going forward. He just hated the idea of any of these grunts profiting from any of it. \'93Now. The Elvi,\'94 he said.\
\'93ELVIS: Putting the slave back in slavery,\'94 Tourism quoted wistfully. \'93Grayling knew how to market.\'94\
\'93I still wonder why we ever emancipated them,\'94 Housing muttered.\
Moral Observance spoke through the crumbs on his lips. \'93It\'92s apparent the Elvi pay no regard for the one true religion. I doubt any of them know the meaning of a balance sheet or a profit statement. And I am most concerned by this Holy-Momma-worship the Elvi are indulging in.\'94\
Gerry diplomatically coughed, and glanced at the CEO. Neither wanted to discuss their virus project in a wider cabinet meeting. \'93There are intelligence efforts currently in progress regarding the Holy Momma.\'94\
\'93I trust you have the initiatives well in hand, Gerry,\'94 Dunhilton prompted.\
\'93Indeed, CEO, I have,\'94 Gerry answered.\
\'93Very well.\'94 Dunhilton cut off Moral Observance\'92s objections with a raised hand. \'93You\'92ve all been briefed on the St Hedges incursion\'97parachutes, aircraft, the Air Force\'92s\'85\'94 he paused meaningfully, \'93\'85difficulties. Defence will be providing a full written report by end of day.\'94\
Defence seemed to collapse from the inside out, like a deflating airbed.\
\'93But the parachute assault was merely delivery,\'94 Dunhilton continued. He stabbed his tablet with his middle finger, which fired up the conference room holo screen. \'93Can anyone tell me how this guy thinks he can upstage the Very Arch Business Bishop of tax-damned Ulyssia?\'94\
A holo-vid resolved in the middle of the board table. The image shook and blurred, steadied, then focused on the ornately dressed figure striding up the nave of St Hedges Cathedral. The High Elvis in full regalia\'97sequinned cape catching light, sunglasses deflecting stained-glass beams across the congregation in calculated bursts of blue and gold. The camera followed him to the dais where the Very Arch Business Bishop d\'92Molesto half-rose from his throne, frozen in the hazy glow.\
\'93Psychological warfare,\'94 Gerry muttered.\
The High Elvis bowed in a studied gesture that felt like mockery, then reached for the gilded staff traditionally reserved for ceremonial blessings.\
The cathedral erupted: \'93Holy Momma! Holy Momma!\'94\
\'93This is where he crosses the line,\'94 Tourism remarked.\
D\'92Molesto adjusted his robes, defeated. The recording ended with chants intensifying into thundering applause.\
\'93What we just witnessed,\'94 Dunhilton said quietly, \'93was a calculated attack on the dignity of our Airborne institutions. A hospitality clone dared to rival the Vicar of Capitalism himself.\'94 His voice dropped. \'93Give me actionable solutions. Are we gods, or are we whittled to shadows?\'94\
The reminder of their fragile standing sent shivers through the directors.\
Defence leaned forward, grateful for something to contribute. \'93Military strike on Clambake. Precision hover-copt assault, minimal collateral\'97\'94\
\'93No.\'94\
The Food Preservation Ombudsman tried. \'93Cut off food shipments, power\'97\'94\
\'93They\'92ve survived worse.\'94\
Moral Observance dabbed his lips. \'93Counter-propaganda. Remind them of the virtues of profit-based spirituality\'97\'94\
\'93They\'92re already worshipping a pregnant woman.\'94\
Corrections: \'93Mass arrests. Round up the leadership\'97\'94\
\'93And make martyrs? No.\'94\
The proposals died. The directors watched Dunhilton, recalibrating.\
\'93Heston,\'94 Dunhilton said softly.\
The Director of Freedom looked up, swallowing hard.\
\'93This situation began with PAPER\'92s failure. Compromised operations, missing bodies.\'94 Dunhilton\'92s voice remained calm, which made it worse. \'93The Elvi formed a government under your watch. They crowned a king under your watch. They infiltrated St Hedges under your watch.\'94\
\'93Your Serene Corporateness, the operation predates my\'97\'94\
Dunhilton raised his voice. \'93The Director of Freedom has regrettably elected to resign.\'94\
\'93What?\'94 Heston What\'92s-His-Face demanded. Everyone knew Defence had been required to write a resignation letter, and were expecting everything to be pinned on him.\
Dunhilton didn\'92t miss a beat. \'93Police Commissioner Hardman will step in as acting Director of Freedom, as well as official Director of Elvi Rights.\'94 Dunhilton shot a gaze through his eyebrows down the table at the stricken ex-director. \'93Oh, sorry, Millicent, you\'92re fired as of thirty minutes ago. Now get out. Both of you get out now, or you\'92ll both be hugging pillows.\'94\
As the two stricken, defrocked ex-cabinet members scurried out\'97Elvi Rights, in her haste, forsook her tablet\'97those remaining in the room made a ceremony of congratulating and backslapping Gerry. Moral Observance finally secured a pastry and gnawed at it nervously. Gerry noted something on his tablet, receiving the most powerful security appointment in Ulyssian history with the ceremony of a coffee order.\
\'93Gerry will assume oversight of PAPER operations effective immediately. Defence, you\'92ll report directly to me until I decide whether to keep you or let you hug a pillow.\'94 Dunhilton stood. \'93We are adjourned.\'94
